## Codex

Use the bundled system `skill-creator` for Codex skill authoring. Check Codex
support itself before treating an OpenAI API feature as a Codex setting.

Proactively delegate useful independent work to the configured efficiency roles
as it arises: `extractor` for facts from specified logs/files/pages, `coder` for
exact mechanical edits with named files and checks, `explorer` for repository
questions, `researcher` for source discovery, `patcher` for bounded
implementation needing judgment, and `verifier` for prescribed checks and edge
cases. These role-specific model assignments are
authorized on every parent model when useful. Preserve the parent model and
reasoning effort; honor explicit task and model requirements.

Prefer direct CLI operations for trivial deterministic work and batch related
mechanical work in one focused assignment. Normally use one or two children,
with non-overlapping ownership. Give each a focused fresh brief
(`fork_turns: "none"` where supported): an explicit cwd, absolute input paths,
owned files or modules, output artifact path or format, and acceptance checks.
Filter large logs and pages before model reading; have parsers write structured
artifacts directly and return compact findings with evidence locations. Escalate on
evidence of a missing contract, scope growth, ownership conflict, or unresolved
check failure rather than repeating generic retries. The parent integrates and
judges the evidence. Keep generic `default`, `worker`, and `reviewer` on parent
inheritance.
